## Why This Is Asked
Rotations are fundamental in cryptography (e.g., SHA-2), hashing, and bitboard manipulation. Implementing them correctly on composite 128-bit types tests understanding of cross-word boundaries and careful handling of edge cases.

## Key Concepts
- Decompose 128-bit value into hi/lo 64-bit halves
- Handle k near 64 where rotation crosses half boundaries
- No loops required—just careful bitwise arithmetic
- Return early for k==0 to avoid undefined behavior with 64-bit shifts

## Code Example
```c
typedef struct { uint64_t hi; uint64_t lo; } uint128;

uint128 rotl128(uint128 x, unsigned k) {
    k &= 127;
    if (k == 0) return x;

    if (k < 64) {
        uint64_t hi = (x.hi << k) | (x.lo >> (64 - k));
        uint64_t lo = (x.lo << k) | (x.hi >> (64 - k));
        return (uint128){hi, lo};
    } else {
        unsigned k2 = k - 64;
        uint64_t hi = (x.lo << k2) | (x.hi >> (64 - k2));
        uint64_t lo = (x.hi << k2) | (x.lo >> (64 - k2));
        return (uint128){hi, lo};
    }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a branchless, efficient 128-bit bit-count using a proven 64-bit SWAR approach on two halves.

## Key Concepts
- SWAR (SIMD Within A Register) popcount on 64-bit chunks
- Treat 128-bit as two independent 64-bit parts
- Branchless, constant-time operations

## Code Example
```javascript
// C-like helper (conceptual)
static inline uint8_t pop64(uint64_t v){
  v -= (v>>1) & 0x5555555555555555ULL;
  v = (v & 0x3333333333333333ULL) + ((v>>2) & 0x3333333333333333ULL);
  v = (v + (v>>4)) & 0x0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0FULL;
  return (v * 0x0101010101010101ULL) >> 56;
}
uint8_t countSetBits128(uint128 x){
  return pop64(x.hi) + pop64(x.lo);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Interleaving bits is a practical pattern in spatial indexing (Morton codes) and graphics. This tests branch-free bit twiddling and understanding of bit spreading.

## Key Concepts
- Bit spreading (part1by1)
- Masked shifts and combiners
- Branch-free composition for 64-bit results

## Code Example
```javascript
uint64_t spread32(uint32_t x){
  uint64_t y = x;
  y = (y | (y << 16)) & 0x0000FFFF0000FFFFULL;
  y = (y | (y << 8))  & 0x00FF00FF00FF00FFULL;
  y = (y | (y << 4))  & 0x0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0FULL;
  y = (y | (y << 2))  & 0x3333333333333333ULL;
  y = (y | (y << 1))  & 0x5555555555555555ULL;
  return y;
}
uint64_t interleave32(uint32_t a, uint32_t b){
  return spread32(a) | (spread32(b) << 1);
}
```

